":{"zh":"dk-breadcrumb-creator是一个用于构建AI智能代理的工具包，不仅仅是编排，还包括周围的工程模式","ja":"dk-breadcrumb-creatorは、AIエージェントをビルドするためのキットであり、オーケストレーションだけでなく、エンジニアリングパターンも含む","ko":"dk-breadcrumb-creator는 AI 에이전트를 빌드하는 툴킷으로, 오케스트레이션뿐만 아니라 周围의 엔지니어링 패턴도 포함","es":"El kit dk-breadcrumb-creator permite desarrollar aplicaciones con Agentes de IA de manera efectiva","fr":"Le kit dk-breadcrumb-creator permet de développer des applications avec des Agents IA de manière efficace","de":"Das Kit dk-breadcrumb-creator ermöglicht die Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit KI-Agenten auf effektive Weise","pt":"O dk-breadcrumb-creator é um kit para construir soluções de IA, incluindo padrões de engenharia","ru":"dk-breadcrumb-creator — это набор для создания решений с ИИ Агентами, включая шаблоны инженерии","ar":"dk-breadcrumb-creator هو حزمة لبناء حلول الذكاء الاصطناعي، بما في ذلك أنماط الهندسة","en":"A kit for building with AI agents — not just the orchestration, but also the engineering patterns around it. "},"definition":{"en":"A kit for building with AI agents — not just the orchestration, but also the engineering patterns around it. "},"features":{"zh":["支持AI智能代理的构建","提供周围的工程模式","易于使用和集成","支持多种开发语言","提供灵活的配置选项"],"ja":["AIエージェントのビルドをサポート","オーケストレーションを超えたエンジニアリングパターンを提供","使用しやすく、統合が簡単","複数の開発言語をサポート","柔軟な設定オプションを提供"],"ko":["AI 에이전트 빌드를 지원","오케스트레이션을 超えた 엔지니어링 패턴을 제공","사용하기 쉽고 통합하기 쉽","複数의 개발 언어를 지원","유연한 설정 옵션을 제공"],"es":["Patrones de ingeniería para Agentes de IA","Orquestación de aplicaciones con Agentes de IA","Desarrollo de aplicaciones con tecnologías como React y Node.js","Integración con herramientas de CLI","Soporte para múltiples plataformas"],"fr":["Modèles d''ingénierie pour les Agents IA","Orchestration d''applications avec des Agents IA","Développement d''applications avec des technologies comme React et Node.js","Intégration avec des outils de CLI","Prise en charge de plusieurs plateformes"],"de":["Ingenieurmuster für KI-Agenten","Orchestrierung von Anwendungen mit KI-Agenten","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit Technologien wie React und Node.js","Integration mit CLI-Tools","Unterstützung für mehrere Plattformen"],"pt":["Criação de ferramentas de IA personalizadas","Padrões de engenharia de IA","Desenvolvimento de soluções de IA","Integração com tecnologias de IA","Otimização de desempenho de IA"],"ru":["Создание индивидуальных инструментов ИИ Агентов","Шаблоны инженерии ИИ","Разработка решений с ИИ Агентами","Интеграция с технологиями ИИ","Оптимизация производительности ИИ"],"ar":["إنشاء أدوات ذكاء اصطناعي مخصصة","أنماط هندسة الذكاء الاصطناعي","تطوير حلول الذكاء الاصطناعي","التكامل مع تقنيات الذكاء الاصطناعي","تحسين أداء الذكاء الاصطناعي"]},"keywords":{"zh":["AI智能代理","dk-breadcrumb-creator","AI工具","如何使用dk-breadcrumb-creator","dk-breadcrumb-creator安装","dk-breadcrumb-creator设置指南","AI智能代理开发","AI工具比较"],"ja":["AIエージェント","dk-breadcrumb-creator","AIツール","dk-breadcrumb-creatorの使用方法","dk-breadcrumb-creatorのインストール","dk-breadcrumb-creatorの設定ガイド","AIエージェント開発","AIツールの比較"],"ko":["AI 에이전트","dk-breadcrumb-creator","AI 툴","dk-breadcrumb-creator 사용 방법","dk-breadcrumb-creator 설치","dk-breadcrumb-creator 설정 가이드","AI 에이전트 개발","AI 툴 비교"],"es":["cómo usar Agentes de IA","qué es un Agente de IA","dk-breadcrumb-creator alternativa","dk-breadcrumb-creator vs otros kits","instalación de dk-breadcrumb-creator","guía de configuración de dk-breadcrumb-creator","desarrollo de aplicaciones con Agentes de IA"],"fr":["comment utiliser des Agents IA","qu''est-ce qu''un Agent IA","dk-breadcrumb-creator alternative","dk-breadcrumb-creator vs autres kits","installation de dk-breadcrumb-creator","guide de configuration de dk-breadcrumb-creator","développement d''applications avec des Agents IA"],"de":["wie man KI-Agenten verwendet","was ist ein KI-Agent","dk-breadcrumb-creator Alternative","dk-breadcrumb-creator vs andere Kits","Installation von dk-breadcrumb-creator","Konfigurationshandbuch für dk-breadcrumb-creator","Entwicklung von Anwendungen mit KI-Agenten"],"pt":["como usar dk-breadcrumb-creator","o que é dk-breadcrumb-creator","dk-breadcrumb-creator alternativa","dk-breadcrumb-creator vs outros","instalar dk-breadcrumb-creator","guia de configuração dk-breadcrumb-creator","desenvolvimento de ia","ferramentas de ia"],"ru":["как использовать dk-breadcrumb-creator","что такое dk-breadcrumb-creator","альтернатива dk-breadcrumb-creator","dk-breadcrumb-creator vs другие","установить dk-breadcrumb-creator","руководство по настройке dk-breadcrumb-creator","разработка ии","инструменты ии"],"ar":["كيفية استخدام dk-breadcrumb-creator","ما هو dk-breadcrumb-creator","بديل dk-breadcrumb-creator","dk-breadcrumb-creator مقارنة بالآخرين","تثبيت dk-breadcrumb-creator","دليل إعداد dk-breadcrumb-creator","تطوير الذكاء الاصطناعي","أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي"]}},"owner":"deepklarity","repo":"harness-kit","repoPath":"deepklarity/harness-kit","stars":1,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-01T21:07:07Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"dk-breadcrumb-creator","description":"Traces a workflow end-to-end through the harness-kit monorepo and creates a breadcrumb analysis doc in docs/breadcrumb_analysis/. Use this skill whenever the user wants to document a flow, trace a workflow, understand how a feature works across layers (frontend → backend → worker → CLI), or create debugging guides for a specific flow. Also use when the user mentions breadcrumb, trace this flow, how does X work end to end, document this workflow, or /dk-breadcrumb-creator.","bodyPreview":"# /dk-breadcrumb-creator — Workflow Breadcrumb Analysis\n\nTraces a workflow through the harness-kit monorepo and produces a compact debugging reference. The output is for devs and agents who need to find where things break — not for onboarding docs or architecture overviews.\n\n## Context\n\n<flow_context> $ARGUMENTS </flow_context>\n\nIf the context above is empty, ask: \"Which flow do you want to trace? Describe it in terms of the user action or system event that kicks it off.\"\n\n## Step 0: Check exist","body":"# /dk-breadcrumb-creator — Workflow Breadcrumb Analysis\n\nTraces a workflow through the harness-kit monorepo and produces a compact debugging reference. The output is for devs and agents who need to find where things break — not for onboarding docs or architecture overviews.\n\n## Context\n\n<flow_context> $ARGUMENTS </flow_context>\n\nIf the context above is empty, ask: \"Which flow do you want to trace? Describe it in terms of the user action or system event that kicks it off.\"\n\n## Step 0: Check existing breadcrumbs\n\nBefore scoping anything, read `docs/breadcrumb_analysis/_INDEX.md` to see what already exists. This file lists every breadcrumb folder and what it traces.\n\nCompare the user''s request against the existing entries and make one of three decisions:\n\n1. **Already covered** — The flow is substantially documented in an existing breadcrumb. Tell the user which one covers it and what it contains. Ask if they want to update/extend that existing doc instead of creating a new one.\n\n2. **Partially overlapping** — An existing breadcrumb covers part of the flow (e.g., user asks about \"task execution\" and `spec-task-lifecycle/02-execute-and-dispatch/` covers the dispatch side but not the harness execution internals). Options:\n   - **Extend** the existing breadcrumb (add sections to its FLOW/DETAILS/DEBUG files, or add a new sub-flow folder)\n   - **Create a new breadcrumb** that covers the non-overlapping portion, cross-referencing the existing one\n\n3. **New territory** — Nothing in the index covers this flow. Proceed to Step 1.\n\nWhen extending an existing breadcrumb, read its current FLOW.md first so you don''t duplicate content. Add new information that complements what''s there — don''t rewrite sections that are already accurate.\n\nWhen creating a new breadcrumb that''s adjacent to an existing one, add cross-references in both directions (a \"See also\" line in the new doc pointing to the existing one, and optionally a note in the existing doc pointing to the new one).\n\nPresent your decision to the user before proceeding. Something like:\n\n```\nExisting breadcrumbs I checked:\n- spec-task-lifecycle/02-execute-and-dispatch — covers DAG dispatch, task status transitions\n- harness-isolation-testing — covers harness CLI construction, MCP config, streaming\n\nYour request overlaps with <X> in these areas: <list>.\nI recommend: <extend existing / create new focused on Y / already covered>.\n```\n\n## Step 1: Scope the flow\n\nBefore touching any code, define the boundaries:\n\n```\nFLOW: <name — short, kebab-case, used as folder name>\nTRIGGER: <what kicks it off — button click, API call, CLI command, cron>\nLAYERS: <which layers it touches — fe, api, celery, odin, db>\nEND STATE: <what the user/system sees when it completes>\n```\n\nIf the flow is large (touches 5+ files per layer, or has multiple independent branches), break it into sub-flows. Each sub-flow gets its own folder. Create a parent `_INDEX.md` that links them.\n\nExample of when to split:\n- \"spec execution\" → split into: `spec-planning`, `spec-task-dispatch`, `spec-task-execution`, `spec-assembly`\n- \"task creation\" → probably fine as one flow (FE form → API → DB → response)\n\nAsk the user to confirm the scope before proceeding.\n\n## Step 2: Trace the flow\n\nWork through each layer the flow touches, in execution order. For each hop, record:\n\n1. **Source file and function** — where the action originates\n2. **What it does** — one line, no fluff\n3. **What it passes** — key data (payload shape, IDs, status values)\n4. **Where it goes next** — the next file/function/service in the chain\n\nUse the codebase directly. Read the actual code. Don''t guess from file names.\n\n### Tracing tips\n\n- **Frontend → Backend**: Search for the API URL in the frontend service files (`src/services/`). Match it to the Django URL conf and view.\n- **Backend → Celery**: Search for `.delay(` or `.apply_async(` calls. Check `config/celery.py` and any `tasks.py` files.\n- **Backend → Odin**: Look for `subprocess` calls to `odin` CLI or check `dag_executor.py` for execution strategy routing.\n- **Odin internals**: Follow from `cli.py` → `orchestrator.py` → harness `execute()` methods.\n- **Signal/hook chains**: Check Django signals, DRF `perform_create`/`perform_update` overrides, and model `save()` methods for side effects.\n\n## Step 3: Create the breadcrumb docs\n\nCreate the folder: `docs/breadcrumb_analysis/<flow-name>/`\n\nGenerate three files:\n\n### File 1: `FLOW.md` — High-level flow\n\nThis is the \"where does data go\" overview. Should be readable in 30 seconds.\n\nFormat:\n\n```markdown\n# <Flow Name>\n\nTrigger: <what starts it>\nEnd state: <what the outcome is>\n\n## Flow\n\n<component/file> :: <function>\n  → <what it sends / does>\n<next component/file> :: <function>\n  → <what it sends / does>\n<next component/file> :: <function>\n  → ...\n\n## Sub-flows\n\n(if applicable — link to sub-flow folders)\n```\n\nExample of the flow notation:\n\n```\nBoardView.tsx :: handleCreateTask()\n  → POST /tasks/ {title, board_id, priority, status}\ntasks/views.py :: TaskViewSet.create()\n  → validates, saves to DB, returns TaskReadSerializer response\ntasks/models.py :: Task.save()\n  → triggers TaskHistory creation via signal\n```\n\nKeep it linear. If there''s branching (e.g., different execution strategies), show each branch with a label:\n\n```\ntasks/dag_executor.py :: maybe_execute_task()\n  → checks ODIN_EXECUTION_STRATEGY\n\n  [strategy=local]\n  dag_executor.py :: _execute_local()\n    → subprocess: odin exec <task_id>\n\n  [strategy=celery_dag]\n  execution/celery_dag.py :: poll_and_execute()\n    → picks up task on next poll cycle (every 5s)\n```\n\n### File 2: `DETAILS.md` — Detailed trace\n\nThis is the \"I need to understand what''s actually happening\" doc. File/function level, with the key logic noted.\n\nFormat:\n\n```markdown\n# <Flow Name> — Detailed Trace\n\n## 1. <Layer/Step Name>\n\n**File**: `path/to/file.py`\n**Function**: `function_name()`\n**Called by**: <what triggers this>\n**Calls**: <what this triggers next>\n\nKey logic:\n- <important conditional, validation, transformation>\n- <side effects — signals, logs, cache updates>\n- <error handling — what happens on failure>\n\nData in: <shape of input>\nData out: <shape of output>\n\n---\n\n## 2. <Next Layer/Step>\n...\n```\n\nInclude only details that matter for debugging. Skip boilerplate (imports, standard DRF validation, obvious CRUD). Focus on:\n- Conditionals that change behavior (if/else branches, feature flags, env vars)\n- Data transformations (where shape changes, fields get renamed, data gets enriched)\n- Side effects (signals, async tasks, external calls)\n- Error paths (what exceptions get raised, what gets logged)\n\n### File 3: `DEBUG.md` — Debugging guide\n\nThis is the \"something broke in this flow, where do I look\" doc.\n\nFormat:\n\n```markdown\n# <Flow Name> — Debug Guide\n\n## Log locations\n\n| Layer | Log file | What''s in it |\n|-------|----------|-------------|\n| Django | `taskit/taskit-backend/logs/taskit_detail.log` | Request/response, view errors |\n| DAG exec | `taskit/taskit-backend/logs/dag_exec_<task_id>.log` | Per-task execution log |\n| Odin | `.odin/logs/run_<run_id>.jsonl` | Structured execution events |\n| Celery | terminal output / broker | Task dispatch and results |\n| Frontend | browser console | API call errors, state updates |\n\n(include only rows relevant to this flow)\n\n## What to search for\n\n| Symptom | Where to look | Search term |\n|---------|--------------|-------------|\n| <common failure mode> | <file or log> | <grep pattern> |\n| <another failure mode> | <file or log> | <grep pattern> |\n\n## Quick commands\n\n```bash\n# <description of what this checks>\n<command>\n\n# <description>\n<command>\n```\n\n## Env vars that affect this flow\n\n| Variable | Effect | Default |\n|----------|--------|---------|\n| <VAR_NAME> | <what it changes in this flow> | <default value> |\n\n## Common breakpoints\n\nWhere to put breakpoints or print statements when debugging this flow:\n\n- `path/to/file.py:function_name()` — <why this is a good breakpoint>\n- `path/to/other.py:other_func()` — <why>\n```\n\n### Quick commands section guidance\n\nInclude commands that are actually useful for this specific flow. Examples:\n\n```bash\n# Check if a task exists and its current state\npython taskit/taskit-backend/testing_tools/task_inspect.py <task_id> --brief\n\n# Tail the backend log filtered to a specific task\ngrep \"task_id\" taskit/taskit-backend/logs/taskit_detail.log | tail -20\n\n# Check celery worker status\ncelery -A config inspect active\n\n# Check what odin logged for a spec run\ncat .odin/logs/run_<id>.jsonl | python -m json.tool\n```\n\nDon''t include generic commands. Every command should be specific to debugging THIS flow.\n\n## Step 4: Verify completeness\n\nBefore finishing, check:\n\n- [ ] Every layer the flow touches has at least one entry in FLOW.md\n- [ ] DETAILS.md covers every hop in FLOW.md with file/function specifics\n- [ ] DEBUG.md has log locations for every layer involved\n- [ ] DEBUG.md has at least 3 \"what to search for\" entries based on realistic failure modes\n- [ ] Quick commands actually work (test them if possible)\n- [ ] No fluff — every line earns its place\n- [ ] `docs/breadcrumb_analysis/_INDEX.md` is updated (new folder → add row to the Flows table AND relevant entries to Quick Navigation)\n\n## Step 5: Output summary\n\nAfter creating the docs, tell the user:\n\n```\nCreated breadcrumb analysis for: <flow name>\nLocation: docs/breadcrumb_analysis/<flow-name>/\nFiles:\n  FLOW.md    — high-level flow (<N> steps)\n  DETAILS.md — detailed trace (<N> sections)\n  DEBUG.md   — debug guide (<N> log sources, <N> search patterns, <N> commands)\n\nUpdated: docs/breadcrumb_analysis/_INDEX.md (added to Flows table + Quick Navigation)\n```\n\nIf you extended an existing breadcrumb rather than creating a new folder, adjust the summary accordingly (mention which files were updated and what was added).\n\n## Style rules\n\nThese docs are dev-to-dev notes. They exist so someone (human or agent) can quickly find where to look when something breaks.\n\n- No intro paragraphs. No \"this document describes...\". Jump straight to content.\n- No emoji, no bold-for-emphasis-everywhere, no decorative headers.\n- Use code formatting for file paths, function names, commands, env vars.\n- One line per concept. If a sentence has \"and\" in it, consider splitting.\n- Prefer tables over prose for structured data (log locations, env vars, search patterns).\n- Use `monospace` for anything that appears in code or terminal.\n- If you''re unsure about something, mark it with `[?]` rather than guessing.\n\n## When to split into sub-flows\n\nSplit when:\n- The flow has distinct phases that can fail independently (planning vs execution vs assembly)\n- Different teams/agents own different parts\n- A single FLOW.md would exceed ~50 lines of flow notation\n\nWhen splitting, create:\n```\ndocs/breadcrumb_analysis/<parent-flow>/\n├── _INDEX.md          # Lists sub-flows, brief description of each, execution order\n├── <sub-flow-1>/\n│   ├── FLOW.md\n│   ├── DETAILS.md\n│   └── DEBUG.md\n└── <sub-flow-2>/\n    ├── FLOW.md\n    ├── DETAILS.md\n    └── DEBUG.md\n```\n\nThe `_INDEX.md` format:\n\n```markdown\n# <Parent Flow Name>\n\nSplit into sub-flows because: <one-line reason>\n\n## Sub-flows (execution order)\n\n1. **<sub-flow-1>** — <what this phase does>\n2. **<sub-flow-2>** — <what this phase does>\n\n## Shared context\n\n<any env vars, config, or state that spans all sub-flows>\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:06:25.015Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Debugging Agents needing workflow tracing and compact debugging references.","zh":"适用于需要工作流跟踪和紧凑的调试参考的调试代理。","ja":"ワークフローのトレースとコンパクトなデバッグ参照が必要なデバッグエージェントに適しています。","ko":"워크플로우 추적 및 컴팩트한 디버깅 참조가 필요한 디버깅 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para agentes de depuración que necesitan trazado de flujo de trabajo y referencias de depuración compactas.","fr":"Parfait pour les agents de débogage nécessitant un traçage du workflow et des références de débogage compactes.","de":"Perfekt für Debugging-Agents, die Workflow-Tracing und kompakte Debugging-Referenzen benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Depuração que necessitam de rastreamento de fluxo de trabalho e referências de depuração compactas.","ru":"Идеально подходит для агентов отладки, которым необходимы отслеживание потока работы и компактные ссылки для отладки.","ar":" مثالي لعميل العامل الذي يحتاج إلى تتبع سير العمل والمراجع المضغوطة للتصحيح."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to trace workflows through the harness-kit monorepo, producing compact debugging references using workflow breadcrumb analysis, ideal for devs and agents needing to identify breakpoints, leveraging context analysis and flow visualization.","zh":"赋予代理通过harness-kit monorepo跟踪工作流的能力，使用工作流breadcrumb分析生成紧凑的调试参考，适合需要识别断点的开发人员和代理，利用上下文分析和流程可视化。","ja":"harness-kit monorepoを通じてワークフローをトレースし、ワークフローブレッドクランブ分析を使用してコンパクトなデバッグ参照を生成するエージェントの能力を与え、ブレークポイントを特定する必要がある開発者とエージェントに最適です。コンテキスト分析とフロー可視化を利用します。","ko":"harness-kit monorepo를 통해 워크플ロー 추적 및 워크플로우 브레드 크럼 분석을 사용하여 컴팩트한 디버깅 참조를 생성하는 에이전트의 능력을 부여하여 브레이크 포인트를 식별해야 하는 개발자 및 에이전트에게 적합합니다. 컨텍스트 분석 및 플로우 시각화를 활용합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a rastrear flujos de trabajo a través del monorepo harness-kit, produciendo referencias de depuración compactas utilizando análisis de migas de pan de flujo de trabajo, ideal para devs y agentes que necesitan identificar puntos de interrupción, aprovechando el análisis de contexto y la visualización de flujo.","fr":"Permet aux agents de tracer les flux de travail à travers le monorepo harness-kit, produisant des références de débogage compactes en utilisant l''analyse de fil d''Ariane du flux de travail, idéal pour les devs et les agents qui doivent identifier les points d''arrêt, en exploitant l''analyse de contexte et la visualisation de flux.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Workflows über das harness-kit-Monorepo zu verfolgen, indem kompakte Debugging-Referenzen unter Verwendung der Workflow-Breadcrumb-Analyse erstellt werden, ideal für Entwickler und Agenten, die Breakpoints identifizieren müssen, unter Ausnutzung von Kontextanalyse und Flussvisualisierung.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a rastrear fluxos de trabalho por meio do repositório monorepo harness-kit, produzindo referências de depuração compactas usando análise de migalhas de fluxo de trabalho, ideal para devs e agentes que precisam identificar pontos de interrupção, aproveitando a análise de contexto e visualização de fluxo.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отслеживать потоки работы через монорепозиторий harness-kit, производя компактные ссылки для отладки с помощью анализа крошек потока работы, идеально подходит для разработчиков и агентов, которым необходимо выявлять точки остановки, используя контекстный анализ и визуализацию потока.","ar":"يمنح الوكلاء khảية تتبع سير العمل من خلال المستودع الفردي harness-kit، لإنتاج مراجع تصحيح مضغوطة باستخدام تحليل الخبز المسلوك في سير العمل، مثالي للمطورين والوكلاء الذين يحتاجون إلى تحديد نقاط التعطل، واستخدام تحليل السياق وتصور التدفق."},"useCases":{"en":["Debugging broken workflows","Tracing system events","Generating compact debugging references"],"zh":["调试损坏的工作流","跟踪系统事件","生成紧凑的调试参考"],"ja":["壊れたワークフローのデバッグ","システムイベントのトレース","コンパクトなデバッグ参照の生成"],"ko":["손상된 워크플로우 디버깅","시스템 이벤트 추적","컴팩트한 디버깅 참조 생성"],"es":["Depuración de flujos de trabajo rotos","Rastreo de eventos del sistema","Generación de referencias de depuración compactas"],"fr":["Débogage de flux de travail cassés","Traçage d''événements système","Génération de références de débogage compactes"],"de":["Fehlerbehebung von fehlerhaften Workflows","Verfolgung von Systemereignissen","Erstellung von kompakten Debugging-Referenzen"],"pt":["Depuração de fluxos de trabalho quebrados","Rastreamento de eventos do sistema","Geração de referências de depuração compactas"],"ru":["Отладка сломанных рабочих потоков","Отслеживание системных событий","Генерация компактных ссылок для отладки"],"ar":["تصحيح سير العمل المكسور","تتبع أحداث النظام","توليد مراجع تصحيح مضغوطة"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires context information","Limited to harness-kit monorepo","Output intended for devs and agents, not for onboarding or architecture overviews"],"zh":["需要上下文信息","仅限harness-kit monorepo","输出适用于开发人员和代理，不适用于入职或架构概述"],"ja":["コンテキスト情報が必要","harness-kit monorepoに限定される","出力は開発者とエージェントのために設計されており、入社またはアーキテクチャ概要には適していない"],"ko":["컨텍스트 정보가 필요","harness-kit monorepo에만 제한","출력은 개발자 및 에이전트를 위해 설계되었으며 입사 또는 아키텍처 개요에는 적합하지 않음"],"es":["Requiere información de contexto","Limitado al monorepo harness-kit","Salida destinada a devs y agentes, no para la incorporación o revisiones de arquitectura"],"fr":["Nécessite des informations de contexte","Limité au monorepo harness-kit","Sortie destinée aux devs et aux agents, et non aux processus d''intégration ou aux revues d''architecture"],"de":["Benötigt Kontextinformationen","Begrenzt auf das harness-kit-Monorepo","Ausgabe für Entwickler und Agenten bestimmt, nicht für Onboarding oder Architekturübersichten"],"pt":["Exige informações de contexto","Limitado ao repositório monorepo harness-kit","Saída destinada a devs e agentes, não para integração ou visões gerais de arquitetura"],"ru":["Требует контекстной информации","Ограничен монорепозиторием harness-kit","Выходные данные предназначены для разработчиков и агентов, не для интеграции или обзоров архитектуры"],"ar":["يتطلب معلومات سياق","محدود بالمستودع الفردي harness-kit","مخرجات مخصصة للمطورين والوكلاء، وليس للترحيل أو لمحة عامة عن الهندسة المعمارية"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"60c29ae71a590ad296356ccb3344de9d6f373b4608457bfeb59c85eb5136d6ed","qualityScore":45}');
