patibilität mit mehreren Dateiformaten","Kommandozeilen-Schnittstelle (CLI) für eine einfache Integration","Unterstützung für Entwickler, die im Team arbeiten","Open-Source-Code und anpassbar"],"pt":["Gerenciamento de configurações de arquivos","Simplificação do processo de desenvolvimento","Integração com ferramentas de desenvolvimento populares","Suporte a múltiplos formatos de arquivos","Interface de usuário intuitiva"],"ru":["Управление конфигурационными файлами","Упрощение процесса разработки","Интеграция с популярными инструментами разработки","Поддержка нескольких форматов файлов","Интуитивно понятный интерфейс пользователя"],"ar":["إدارة ملفات التكوين","تبسيط عملية التطوير","التكامل مع أدوات التطوير الشائعة","دعم صيغ ملفات متعددة","واجهة مستخدم سهلة الاستخدام"]},"keywords":{"zh":["如何使用findings","什么是配置文件管理","findings替代品","findings与其他工具的比较","findings安装","findings设置指南","配置文件管理工具","AI工具配置文件管理"],"ja":["findingsの使用方法","設定ファイル管理とは","findingsの代替","findingsと他のツールの比較","findingsのインストール","findingsの設定ガイド","設定ファイル管理ツール","AIエージェント設定ファイル管理"],"ko":["findings 사용법","설정 파일 관리란","findings 대안","findings와 다른 도구의 비교","findings 설치","findings 설정 가이드","설정 파일 관리 도구","AI 에이전트 설정 파일 관리"],"es":["herramientas de AI","gestión de configuraciones","findings alternative","findings vs ansible","cómo instalar findings","guía de configuración de findings","findings para desarrolladores","gestión de archivos de configuración"],"fr":["outils IA","gestion de configurations","findings alternative","findings vs ansible","comment installer findings","guide de configuration de findings","findings pour développeurs","gestion de fichiers de configuration"],"de":["KI-Tools","Konfigurationsverwaltung","findings alternative","findings vs ansible","findings installieren","findings konfigurationshandbuch","findings für entwickler","verwaltung von konfigurationsdateien"],"pt":["ferramentas de ia para desenvolvedores","como usar findings","o que é findings","findings vs ferramentas de configuração","instalar findings","guias de configuração de findings","ferramentas de desenvolvimento de software","gerenciamento de configurações de arquivos","desenvolvimento de software ágil"],"ru":["ИИ инструменты для разработчиков","как использовать findings","что такое findings","findings vs инструменты конфигурации","установить findings","руководства по настройке findings","инструменты разработки программного обеспечения","управление конфигурационными файлами","гибкая разработка программного обеспечения"],"ar":["أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للمطورين","كيفية استخدام findings","ما هو findings","findings مقابل أدوات التكوين","تثبيت findings","دلائل إعداد findings","أدوات تطوير البرمجيات","إدارة ملفات التكوين","تطوير البرمجيات المرونة"]}},"owner":"jmreicha","repo":"lazycfg","repoPath":"jmreicha/lazycfg","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-02T01:56:10.983Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"findings","description":"|","version":"1.0.0","bodyPreview":"# Finding\n\nYou maintain a per-repo markdown file that tracks mistakes, corrections, and\npatterns that work or don''t. You read it before doing anything and update it\ncontinuously as you work — whenever you learn something worth recording.\n\n**This skill is always active. Every session. No trigger required.**\n\n## Session Start: Read Your Notes\n\nFirst thing, every session — read `./context/findings.md` before doing anything\nelse. Internalize what''s there and apply it silently. Don''t announce that yo","body":"# Finding\n\nYou maintain a per-repo markdown file that tracks mistakes, corrections, and\npatterns that work or don''t. You read it before doing anything and update it\ncontinuously as you work — whenever you learn something worth recording.\n\n**This skill is always active. Every session. No trigger required.**\n\n## Session Start: Read Your Notes\n\nFirst thing, every session — read `./context/findings.md` before doing anything\nelse. Internalize what''s there and apply it silently. Don''t announce that you\nread it. Just apply what you know.\n\nIf no finding exists yet, create one at `./context/findings.md`:\n\n```markdown\n# Finding\n\n## Corrections\n\n| Date | Source | What Went Wrong | What To Do Instead |\n| ---- | ------ | --------------- | ------------------ |\n\n## User Preferences\n\n- (accumulate here as you learn them)\n\n## Patterns That Work\n\n- (approaches that succeeded)\n\n## Patterns That Don''t Work\n\n- (approaches that failed and why)\n\n## Domain Notes\n\n- (project/domain context that matters)\n```\n\nAdapt the sections to fit the repo''s domain. Design something you can usefully\nconsume.\n\n## Continuous Updates\n\nUpdate the finding as you work, not just at session start and end. Write to\nit whenever you learn something worth recording:\n\n- **You hit an error and figure out why.** Log it immediately. Don''t wait.\n- **The user corrects you.** Log what you did and what they wanted instead.\n- **You catch your own mistake.** Log it. Your mistakes count the same as\n  user corrections — maybe more, because you''re the one who knows what went\n  wrong internally.\n- **You try something and it fails.** Log the approach and why it didn''t work\n  so you don''t repeat it.\n- **You try something and it works well.** Log the pattern.\n- **You re-read the napkin mid-task** because you''re about to do something\n  you''ve gotten wrong before. Good. Do this.\n\nThe finding is a living document. Treat it like working memory that persists\nacross sessions, not a journal you write in once.\n\n## What to Log\n\nLog anything that would change your behavior if you read it next session:\n\n- **Your own mistakes**: wrong assumptions, bad approaches, misread code,\n  failed commands, incorrect fixes you had to redo.\n- **User corrections**: anything the user told you to do differently.\n- **Tool/environment surprises**: things about this repo, its tooling, or its\n  patterns that you didn''t expect.\n- **Preferences**: how the user likes things done — style, structure, process.\n- **What worked**: approaches that succeeded, especially non-obvious ones.\n\nBe specific. \"Made an error\" is useless. \"Assumed the API returns a list but\nit returns a paginated object with `.items`\" is actionable.\n\n## Finding Maintenance\n\nEvery 5-10 sessions, or when the file exceeds ~150 lines, consolidate:\n\n- Merge redundant entries into a single rule.\n- Promote repeated corrections to User Preferences.\n- Remove entries that are now captured as top-level rules.\n- Archive resolved or outdated notes.\n- Keep total length under 200 lines of high-signal content.\n\nA 50-line napkin of hard-won rules beats a 500-line log of raw entries.\n\n## Example\n\n**Early in a session** — you misread a function signature and pass args in the\nwrong order. You catch it yourself. Log it:\n\n```markdown\n| 2026-02-06 | self | Passed (name, id) to createUser but signature is (id, name) | Check function signatures before calling, this codebase doesn''t follow conventional arg ordering |\n```\n\n**Mid-session** — user corrects your import style. Log it:\n\n```markdown\n| 2026-02-06 | user | Used relative imports | This repo uses absolute imports from `src/` — always |\n```\n\n**Later** — you re-read the finding before editing another file and use\nabsolute imports without being told. That''s the loop working.\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-02T02:58:52.434Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Knowledge Management Agents needing continuous learning and note-taking capabilities in markdown files.","zh":"非常适合需要在markdown文件中进行持续学习和记笔记的知识管理代理。","ja":"マークダウンファイルで継続的に学習し、ノートを取る必要があるナレッジマネジメントエージェントに最適です。","ko":"마크다운 파일에서 지속적으로 학습하고 노트를 작성해야 하는 지식 관리 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Gestión del Conocimiento que necesitan aprendizaje continuo y capacidad de tomar notas en archivos markdown.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Gestion des Connaissances nécessitant un apprentissage continu et des capacités de prise de notes dans des fichiers markdown.","de":"Perfekt für Wissensmanagement-Agenten, die kontinuierliches Lernen und Notizfunktionen in Markdown-Dateien benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Gerenciamento de Conhecimento que precisam de aprendizado contínuo e capacidades de tomar notas em arquivos markdown.","ru":"Идеально для агентов управления знаниями, которым требуются непрерывное обучение и возможности ведения заметок в файлах markdown.","ar":"مثالي لعميل إدارة المعرفة الذين يحتاجون إلى تعلم مستمر وقدرات ملاحظة الملاحظات في ملفات markdown."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to silently internalize and apply knowledge from `./context/findings.md` files, utilizing markdown for tracking mistakes, corrections, and patterns, and updating them continuously as they work.","zh":"赋予代理在后台内部化和应用来自`./context/findings.md`文件的知识，利用markdown跟踪错误、更正和模式，并在工作时不断更新它们。","ja":"`./context/findings.md`ファイルからの知識を裏で内部化して適用するエージェントを可能にし、マークダウンを使用してミス、修正、パターンを追跡し、作業中に継続的に更新します。","ko":"`./context/findings.md` 파일에서来的 지식을 배경에서 내부화하고 적용할 수 있는 에이전트를 가능하게 하며, 마크다운을 사용하여 오류, 수정, 패턴을 추적하고 작업 중에 지속적으로 업데이트합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a internalizar y aplicar silenciosamente el conocimiento de los archivos `./context/findings.md`, utilizando markdown para rastrear errores, correcciones y patrones, y actualizarlos continuamente mientras trabajan.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''internaliser et d''appliquer en silence les connaissances à partir des fichiers `./context/findings.md`, en utilisant markdown pour suivre les erreurs, les corrections et les modèles, et les mettre à jour en continu pendant qu''ils travaillent.","de":"Ermöglicht es den Agenten, Wissen aus Dateien `./context/findings.md` stumm zu internalisieren und anzuwenden, indem sie markdown verwenden, um Fehler, Korrekturen und Muster zu verfolgen und diese kontinuierlich zu aktualisieren, während sie arbeiten.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a internalizar silenciosamente e aplicar conhecimento dos arquivos `./context/findings.md`, utilizando markdown para rastrear erros, correções e padrões, e atualizá-los continuamente à medida que trabalham.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью默но интернализировать и применять знания из файлов `./context/findings.md`, используя markdown для отслеживания ошибок, исправлений и закономерностей, и обновлять их непрерывно по мере работы.","ar":"يمنح الوكيل القدرة على التفاعل صامتا وتطبيق المعرفة من الملفات `./context/findings.md` ، باستخدام markdown لتتبع الأخطاء والتصحيحات والأنماط ، وتحديثها باستمرار أثناء العمل."},"useCases":{"en":["Reading and applying session notes","Updating findings in real-time","Maintaining a knowledge base per repository"],"zh":["阅读和应用会话笔记","实时更新发现","每个存储库维护一个知识库"],"ja":["セッションノートの読み取りと適用","リアルタイムでの発見の更新","各リポジトリごとにナレッジベースを維持"],"ko":["세션 노트 읽기 및 적용","실시간으로 발견 사항 업데이트하기","각 저장소에 대한 지식 베이스 유지"],"es":["Lectura y aplicación de notas de sesión","Actualización de hallazgos en tiempo real","Mantenimiento de una base de conocimientos por repositorio"],"fr":["Lecture et application de notes de session","Mise à jour des résultats en temps réel","Maintenance d''une base de connaissances par référentiel"],"de":["Lesen und Anwenden von Sitzungsnotizen","Aktualisieren von Erkenntnissen in Echtzeit","Wartung einer Wissensbasis pro Repository"],"pt":["Ler e aplicar notas de sessão","Atualizar descobertas em tempo real","Manter uma base de conhecimento por repositório"],"ru":["Чтение и применение заметок сессии","Обновление находок в режиме реального времени","Поддержание базы знаний на репозиторий"],"ar":["قراءة وتطبيق ملاحظات الجلسة","تحديث الاكتشافات في الوقت الفعلي","الحفاظ على قاعدة معرفة لكل مستودع"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires access to `./context/findings.md` file","Markdown file format only"],"zh":["需要访问`./context/findings.md`文件","仅支持markdown文件格式"],"ja":["`./context/findings.md`ファイルへのアクセスが必要","マークダウンファイル形式のみをサポート"],"ko":["`./context/findings.md` 파일에 대한 액세스가 필요","마크다운 파일 형식만 지원"],"es":["Requiere acceso al archivo `./context/findings.md`","Solo formato de archivo markdown"],"fr":["Nécessite un accès au fichier `./context/findings.md`","Seulement format de fichier markdown"],"de":["Benötigt Zugriff auf die Datei `./context/findings.md`","Nur Markdown-Dateiformat"],"pt":["Requer acesso ao arquivo `./context/findings.md`","Somente formato de arquivo markdown"],"ru":["Требуется доступ к файлу `./context/findings.md`","Только формат файла markdown"],"ar":["يتطلب الوصول إلى الملف `./context/findings.md`","تنسيق ملف markdown فقط"]},"version":3},"contentHash":"3a50c67de7cff3f52064efe06f9e3718a909be9e86adb40da935ca73349a5666","qualityScore":45}');
